{
  "fileColumn": false,
  "stacked": true,
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "ui-overlays",
      "title": "Spell UI · Overlays",
      "description": "Modals, flyouts, sidebars, dimmers, popups, toasts, nags, transitions.  Today a cancelable `ui-open` / `ui-close` comes first, then `ui-show` / `ui-hide` once the animation ends:  each pair is ONE pair now, `opening / opened`, both rows saying it."
    },
    {
      "id": "ui-folds",
      "title": "Spell UI · Folds, tabs, shapes",
      "description": "`<ui-section>` already sends both halves, `ui-opening` / `ui-opened`;  the accordion, the shape and the tab gain the half they lack."
    },
    {
      "id": "ui-forms",
      "title": "Spell UI · Forms and values",
      "description": "A value changing as you type or drag, a change committed, a form's validation and saving.  Every change is `changing / changed`;  a failure is `<verb>ing failed`."
    },
    {
      "id": "ui-lists",
      "title": "Spell UI · Lists, menus, labels, messages, tables",
      "description": "An item chosen, a label removed, a message dismissed, a column sorted, progress."
    },
    {
      "id": "ui-page",
      "title": "Spell UI · Loading, the page, scrolling",
      "description": "The root getting ready, files loading and saving (the source layer every `source` element shares), code coloured, scrolling into view, sticking."
    },
    {
      "id": "ui-docs",
      "title": "Spell UI · The docs site's widgets",
      "description": "The `<ui-docs-*>` elements the components pages are built from:  not components a program would use, but the same event names."
    },
    {
      "id": "app-elements",
      "title": "spell-app · Its elements",
      "description": "`<spell-app>` (to be `<spell-viewer>`, Q16) and `<spell-editor>`:  a component pack's events keep their own names, never translated."
    },
    {
      "id": "app-runner",
      "title": "spell-app · The runner's drag and drop",
      "description": "Spell's own drag (`Dragging`) sends the web's drag events, so a page can follow it as it would the browser's.  Platform names:  the recommendation spells them as spell would say them, `drag start`, as `mouse down`."
    },
    {
      "id": "app-layout",
      "title": "spell-app · Event words in a layout",
      "description": "The words a handler says today, `when clicked:` or `on-click=` / `when-clicked=` on a tag in a layout.  Handler words follow the events they catch:  a pair's handler can catch either half."
    },
    {
      "id": "spell-code",
      "title": "Spell code · What a program sends and catches",
      "description": "The language's own event words (spell-parser):  `trigger` / `fire` / `send` and `on`, the drop event, the console's, `when created`."
    },
    {
      "id": "epic-elements",
      "title": "spell-epic · The epic pages' elements",
      "description": "The `<epic-*>` pack:  a pack's events keep their own names (`epic-...`), except those it shares with Spell UI (`ui-open`, `ui-change`, `ui-filter`)."
    },
    {
      "id": "epic-pages",
      "title": "spell-epic and the kit · Docs pages and the page server",
      "description": "Window and document events the docs runtime, the site's router and the page server's live client send.  `spell-site:*` and `spell-server:*` are the kit's page server's, which spell-epic's pages listen for."
    }
  ],
